WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 3.4 · Structure, Governance & Accountability
Board and management responsibilities

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Agree which decisions all co-founders must take together now, and which belong to your board later.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.022
The board, or the founders before one exists, sets direction and oversees. Management proposes plans and runs the work. Reserved matters are decisions only the governing body, or all co-founders together, can take.

4
00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.022
Three tools for clear oversight

5
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:40.093
Reserved matters: A written list of decisions that all co-founders, and later the board, must take together. For example: At the repair café, any loan or new lease needs both founders' agreement.

6
00:00:40.093 --> 00:00:52.163
Governance calendar: Fixed dates in the year to review strategy, budget, accounts, risks and policies. For example: The bakery founders review the accounts in March and set next year's budget in October.

7
00:00:52.163 --> 00:01:05.433
Two hats, recorded: A record of when a founder acts as manager and when as board member. For example: Minutes note that the founder left the room while her own pay was discussed.

8
00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:06.433
Why it matters

9
00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:12.107
1. It stops one founder deciding alone on things that affect everyone.

10
00:01:12.107 --> 00:01:16.670
2. Oversight becomes routine, not a reaction to problems.

11
00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:22.604
3. Someone can safely raise concerns about a founder's work.

12
00:01:23.004 --> 00:01:23.604
What it guides

13
00:01:23.604 --> 00:01:28.537
1. Your delegation of authority: what sits above every limit.

14
00:01:28.537 --> 00:01:33.841
2. Your founders' agreement and, later, your board's terms of reference.

15
00:01:33.841 --> 00:01:39.774
3. How others decide the founder's role and any pay.

16
00:01:40.174 --> 00:01:40.774
What to avoid

17
00:01:40.774 --> 00:01:46.078
A board that manages daily work instead of overseeing it.

18
00:01:46.078 --> 00:01:51.011
Founders taking decisions that now belong to the board.

19
00:01:51.011 --> 00:01:58.056
Leaving the founder's own pay and role for the founder to decide.

20
00:01:58.656 --> 00:02:00.456
You list your reserved matters and draft a first-year governance calendar.

21
00:02:00.456 --> 00:02:04.456
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:05.956 --> 00:02:09.056
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
